  "worked_solution": "A partition of a set $C$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $C$ where every element of $C$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nOf the given collections, only ${{0},{1,2,3\u2026,50}}$ is a partition.\n\nThe rest of the collections are not partitions:\n\n- ${\u2205,{0,1,2,\u2026,50}}$ is not a partition because the subset $\u2205$ is empty.\n\n- ${{0,1,2,\u2026,15},{26,27,28,\u2026,50}}$ is not a partition because the elements $16,17,18,\u2026,25$ do not appear in any subsets.\n\n- ${{0,1,2,\u2026,10},{10,11,12,\u2026,50}}$ is not a partition because the element $10$  appears in both subsets.\n\n- ${{0,1,2,\u2026,8},{10,11,12,\u2026,50}}$ is not a partition because the element $9$ does not appear in any subsets.",
